    "turn_text": "really, no, seriously. Because I wanted to write, the title is superheroes everywhere. And I grew up reading comic books. I love comic books. I'm a nerd. I pretend not to be. And there are so many now movies, superheroes. And I wanted to make the point to all of us, because truly this applies to adults as well. that you don't have to look at a CGI screen to see a superhero. And for children in particular, I wanted to make the point that you're surrounded by superheroes. And if you look closely enough, you can see that they're wearing a cape. And it may be your parent, and I talk about my mother and my father. It may be your grandparent, and I talk about them. I talk about teachers or superheroes. My first great teacher My first great teacher, Mrs. Francis Wilson, attended my law school graduation. I talk about best friends or heroes. And I just think it's really important that as we raise our children, the children of us as a community, that we remind them of how special they are, and that they are surrounded by superheroes. And then the last page of the book, actually, and I'm just going to point it to all of you, And then it's like heroes are you. And it's for them to look and see a picture of themselves. In any event.",
